{
	# Home upgrades. Two kinds:
	#   furniture: an item (special_items.csv row "lls_<id>", tag lls_furniture). Right-click it in your cargo to put
	#     it into your furniture storage (0.5.0), then drag it into a home's furniture slots ("slots" in tiers.json)
	#     on the Furniture tab. A home holds one of each piece.
	#   upgrade: bought with credits on the Upgrades tab, done at once (0.5.0), stays with the home. No slots: a home
	#     can have every upgrade that fits it, except ones that conflict. cost: share of the home's full value, at
	#     least minCost.
	#
	# Effects, the same words house traits use (house_traits.json):
	#   comfort, decor, happiness, health, security (added), price (multiplies the value), wear (multiplied)
	#   valueShare: adds a flat value instead, this share of what it cost (air conditioning, window bars)
	#   levels: home levels it changes, {"heat":-1} cooler, {"radiation":-2} shielded (levels.json)
	#   env: environment scores it changes, {"noise":20} quieter, {"air":15} cleaner (environment.json)
	#   kids: effects only for tenants with kids ("Family with kids"), {"happiness":4}
	#   events: multiplies the chance of events (tenant_events.json), {"small_fire":0.5}
	#   tags: what tenants can like or hate (tenant_traits.json)
	# Where it can go: minTier, maxTier (0 shack to 5 estate), station (true stations only, false planets only),
	#   needs (house traits: only homes with one of them). conflicts: upgrades it never shares a home with.
	# fixes: house traits it removes. oneTime: a job, not a part of the home: gone once done.
	# roll: upgrades a home for sale may already have, like house traits: weight, anyCondition, climates.
	# Chance a home for sale comes with one upgrade already done.
	"listingChance":0.3,
	# Furniture pieces each market with a property agent stocks in its open market, and how often it restocks.
	"shopStock":[1, 3],
	"shopDays":30,
	# Chance that salvage or battle loot holds one piece of furniture.
	"lootChance":0.12,
